The task is: Mark WEB-1 "Checkout button broken" as completed on Friday, September 25, 2026.

What I need to do:
1. Find the issue WEB-1 and get its ID
2. Find the workflow state corresponding to "Completed" (probably in the workflow of the WEB team)
3. Update the issue to the completed state, and set the target date (or startDate?) to 2026-09-25

In Linear, issues have a `targetDate` field. "Completed on Friday, September 25, 2026" — I'll set targetDate to 2026-09-25 and set state to Completed.

First, let me query the issue by identifier.

The Linear GraphQL API:

```graphql
query {
  issue(identifier: "WEB-1") {
    id
    identifier
    title
    state { id name }
    targetDate
  }
}
```

Next, get the workflow states of the team that owns the issue:

```graphql
query {
  team(id: "<teamId>") {
    workflowStates { id name type }
  }
}
```

After that, update:

```graphql
mutation {
  issueUpdate(input: { id: "<issueId>", stateId: "<completedStateId>", targetDate: "2026-09-25" }) {
    success
  }
}
```

Note: September 25, 2026 is indeed a Friday. Let me verify: January 1, 2026 is a Thursday. No, let me calculate. 2026: January 1, 2026... 2025-01-01 was a Wednesday. 2025 is not a leap year (365 days), so 2026-01-01 is a Thursday. Days up to September 25: Jan 31, Feb 28, Mar 31, Apr 30, May 31, Jun 30, Jul 31, Aug 31 = 243 days, plus 25 = day of year 268. Day of week: Jan 1 = Thursday (day 1). (268-1) mod 7 = 267 mod 7 = 267 = 7*38 + 1 → 1. Thursday + 1 = Friday. Yes, September 25, 2026 is a Friday. Good.

Let me start with the first query. I'll use curl against https://api.linear.app/graphql with a Bearer <TOKEN>.

Let me execute step 1.

